From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:50:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: disable the clocks if the core rate restore
 fails on resume

dpu_runtime_resume() returns the error from dev_pm_opp_set_rate() after
clk_bulk_prepare_enable() has already enabled the DPU clocks, so a failed
resume leaves them prepared and enabled. Disable them on that path.

Follows "drm/msm/dpu: Reassert core clock rate on runtime resume"
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
index 23e0a5b2ca22..453b9ef3787d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
@@ -1477,6 +1477,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused dpu_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		if (rc) {
 			DPU_ERROR("failed to restore core clock rate %lu: %d\n",
 				  core_rate, rc);
+			clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(dpu_kms->num_clocks,
+						   dpu_kms->clocks);
 			return rc;
 		}
 		dpu_kms->perf.core_clk_rate = core_rate;
